----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This is an unofficial fork of openMSX, branch 'makoto'
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

This branch adds emulation of Makoto, a sound cartridge for the MSX with a
Yamaha YM2608 (OPNA). There is no real hardware to compare with; the
emulation follows the chip and the cartridge as far as they are known.

Upstream openMSX does not contain any of this. Report problems to this fork,
not to the openMSX developers.

    this fork: https://github.com/madscient/openMSX_Y8960
    upstream:  https://github.com/openMSX/openMSX

What is added
-------------

The cartridge is the extension Makoto (share/extensions/Makoto.xml). It
uses I/O ports only and does not take a cartridge slot:

    openmsx -machine <machine> -ext Makoto

It has one YM2608 at 8 MHz on I/O ports 14h-17h: FM 6 channels, SSG 3
channels, rhythm 6 sounds and ADPCM 1 channel with 256KB of sample RAM.
The sample RAM size is set with <sampleram> (in KB) in the extension file.
The chip's interrupt output is connected to the MSX.

For debugging, the registers are readable as the debuggable "Makoto regs"
(512 bytes, 000h-0FFh the first register array and 100h-1FFh the second,
holding the last value written) and the sample RAM as "Makoto ADPCM RAM".

The rhythm ROM
--------------

The rhythm part plays samples from a ROM inside the YM2608. That ROM is not
included. To hear the rhythm part, put a dump of it in the systemroms
directory, as for other system ROMs (see "System ROMs" in
doc/manual/setup.html):

    size  8192 bytes
    SHA1  50b6c3e288eaa12ad275d4f323267bb72b0445df

openMSX finds it by its SHA1, so the file name and the subdirectory do not
matter. Without it, openMSX shows a warning when the extension is loaded
and the rhythm part stays silent; everything else works.

Known limitations
-----------------

    - On real hardware, reading the status at port 14h collides on the bus
      with a Philips Music Module when one is also connected. This is not
      emulated.
    - The sound is output as two channels: FM + rhythm + ADPCM in stereo,
      and the SSG in mono.

Credits
-------

The YM2608 is emulated by ymfm by Aaron Giles, under the BSD 3-Clause
license. Its copyright notice and license text are in
src/3rdparty/ymfm/LICENSE in the source, and in doc/ymfm-LICENSE.txt in
the Windows package.

The I/O ports and the clock of the cartridge are taken from the Makoto
driver of vgmplay-msx.

